 | workstreams | `tracker.sh workstreams <R-id>` | read-only plan for parallel execution (execute-raft Phase 2B): issues in waves from `depends_on` and overlapping Touched modules, and a last line `parallel: yes (wave k: …)` or `parallel: no` |
 | launch | `tracker.sh launch <R-id\|name> [-- cmd…]` | `worktree`, then runs the command (default `claude`) in that worktree with `exec`: terminal, signals and exit status are native. Refuses an unusable command or worktree path before anything starts |
-| board | `tracker.sh board [--out PATH] [--open]` | writes the whole tracker as one self-contained HTML page, `.cache/board.html` by default (gitignored; regenerate to refresh). Tabs Active / Waiting / Done (Waiting lists only rafts with no unfinished dependency), cursor keys, `/` then an id to jump to it, each raft's issues and dependencies rendered with the vendored marked. `--open` opens it in the browser. `.github/workflows/board.yml` rebuilds it on every push to `main` and keeps it as the `tracker-board` Actions artifact: `rm -rf .cache/board-ci && gh run download -n tracker-board -D .cache/board-ci` fetches the latest into a fresh directory (gh won't overwrite an existing file, and `.cache/board.html` is the local default). On `main`, Active is empty: rafts move to `active/` only on their branch |
+| board | `tracker.sh board [--out PATH] [-O]` | writes the whole tracker as one self-contained HTML page, `.cache/board.html` by default (gitignored; regenerate to refresh). Tabs Active / Waiting / Done (Waiting lists only rafts with no unfinished dependency), cursor keys, `/` then an id to jump to it, each raft's issues and dependencies rendered with the vendored marked. Then it opens the page in the default browser unless `-O` is given (`-O` only writes it, as CI and the specs do; `--open`, the old opt-in, is still accepted and is the default). `.github/workflows/board.yml` rebuilds it on every push to `main` and keeps it as the `tracker-board` Actions artifact: `rm -rf .cache/board-ci && gh run download -n tracker-board -D .cache/board-ci` fetches the latest into a fresh directory (gh won't overwrite an existing file, and `.cache/board.html` is the local default). On `main`, Active is empty: rafts move to `active/` only on their branch |
 | prune | `tracker.sh worktree-prune` | removes the worktree and branch of every raft that is in `done/` on `origin/main` (any merge strategy); keeps the rest, never forces, and lists named worktrees |
 | focus | `tracker.sh focus f0010` | the following commits are attributed to that issue |
 | commit | `tracker.sh commit -m "msg" [--issue f0010]... [--time 25]` | `git add -A`, then records spend rows in each issue's `spend.md` and the raft's summary **in the same commit**, adds `Issue:` trailers, and pushes |
